# Audit report — global descent, pair surface, and reset ownership

Date: 2026-08-10
Base: `eca93e1395c2f690f8357f015ea5901fec9f8310`
Preregistration commit: `6c11c218`

## Result

The pinned 24-branch corpus contains more of the observer-relation skeleton than the earlier
transition audit alone showed, but no branch owns the whole descended physical relation.

The bounded landing is:

```text
GLOBAL_PAIR_FOLIATION_AND_PATH_FUNCTOR_PARTIALLY_OWNED;
CLOCK_ONLY_ENDPOINT_DESCENT_OWNED_ON_A_DIFFERENT_CONTROL;
CARRIED_TO_INTRINSIC_CALIBRATION_RESET_AND_COMPLETE_PAIR_SELECTOR_OPEN;
NO_COMPLETE_DESCENT_SELECTOR_IN_PINNED_CORPUS.
```

This is not a no-go theorem for the metric, time-live branches, or on-shell/global-completion
equations.

## What is newly consolidated

R17/W01 closes a seam that older documents still described as open: on every supplied regular
stationary C01-C06 member, its intrinsic reciprocal plane is globally integrable. The leaves are
`R x S1` Hopf cylinders and the angular screen is their global nonintegrable normal bundle. R17 also
owns an exact path-labelled projected connection, full path composition, and classified holonomy.

But the arrived path-carried projector state is generically not the projector state independently
rebuilt from the metric at the middle observer. The metric owns the full `SO(2)` alignment bitorsor
between them, not one calibration-bearing representative. Thus the physical reset, leaf/path query,
and complete pair selector remain open.

R18/W02 independently owns a clean clock-only endpoint descent on one shared timelike Killing clock state. Its
middle object and identity carry compose exactly. It does not own a ruler, reciprocal pair surface,
or terminal complete-pair depth. R17 and R18 cannot be silently spliced across branches.

R23 owns complete-coframe isometric path transport and holonomy but no non-isometric calibration
scale. R24 owns set-equivariant projector transport, not one selected line or reciprocal density.
R04 remains an aggregate of inequivalent members; its corrected terminal reciprocal cell remains
`INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE`.

