# Exact derivation — R17 intrinsic pair foliation and normal bundle

Date: 2026-08-10

Mode: metric-led, exact analytic/CPU

Current grade: **VERIFIED-WITH-CAVEATS; EXTERNAL ADVERSARIAL REVIEW ACCEPTED**

## 1. Bounded result

On each supplied smooth regular off-shell R17/W01 configuration C01--C06, the complete metric's
intrinsic clock and twist-ruler plane is not merely a pointwise projector. It is a globally
integrable rank-two distribution. Its maximal leaves are Hopf cylinders `R x S1`, and the complete
spacetime is foliated by this family over `S2`.

The angular screen does the opposite: in four dimensions it is a global positive nonintegrable
rank-two normal bundle. On each spatial `S3` slice it is the contact plane. Thus the complete metric
naturally separates into an integrable reciprocal backbone and a twisted angular normal bundle.

Every reciprocal leaf inherits the complete two-metric

```text
h=-u^-2(dt+a dpsi)^2+u^2 dpsi^2,       u=exp(phi),
```

including the nonzero twist. Its determinant is exactly `-1`. The terminal pair evaluator therefore
returns `phi` pointwise and the relative scalar is

```text
delta_K(p,q)=phi(q)-phi(p)=log[N(p)/N(q)].
```

This supplies a global conditional endpoint scalar on R17 because the intrinsic Killing state is
shared over the whole configuration. It does not supply one physical connecting surface for
cross-leaf endpoints, one winding, or the complete path-independent four-dimensional arrow.

Preregistered landing:

```text
GLOBAL_PAIR_FOLIATION_AND_SCALAR_DEPTH_DERIVED__FULL_NORMAL_BUNDLE_ARROW_OPEN
```

## 2. Exact dual frame

Write

```text
theta0=u^-1(dt+a sigma3),
theta1=u sigma3,
theta2=v sigma1,
theta3=v sigma2,
u=exp(phi)>0,
v=exp(lambda phi)>0.
```

Let `(T,Z,X,Y)` be dual to `(dt,sigma3,sigma1,sigma2)`. Exact matrix inversion gives

```text
e0=u T,
e1=u^-1(Z-a T),
e2=v^-1 X,
e3=v^-1 Y.
```

Consequently

```text
E=span(e0,e1)=span(T,Z),
H=span(e2,e3)=span(X,Y).
```

No frozen polynomial coefficient enters these identities.

## 3. Frobenius classification

The Maurer--Cartan equations are

```text
d sigma1=-2 sigma2 wedge sigma3,
d sigma2=-2 sigma3 wedge sigma1,
d sigma3=-2 sigma1 wedge sigma2,
```

so, in the chosen convention,

```text
[X,Y]=2Z,  [Y,Z]=2X,  [Z,X]=2Y,
[T,Z]=[T,X]=[T,Y]=0.
```

For a general stationary `phi`, set

```text
p1=Z(phi), p2=X(phi), p3=Y(phi).
```

Direct bracket algebra gives

```text
[e0,e1]=-(p1/u)e0.
```

There is no `e2` or `e3` component. Therefore `E` is involutive for every smooth stationary profile,
for every supplied `lambda`, and for every nonzero supplied twist `a`. This is not an artifact of
the frozen C01--C06 polynomial.

For the screen,

```text
[e2,e3]
 =2a/(u v^2)e0 + 2u/v^2 e1
  +(lambda p3/v)e2 -(lambda p2/v)e3.
```

The `e1` coefficient is nonzero everywhere on the regular stratum because `u,v>0`. Hence `H` is
not Frobenius integrable. In four dimensions it is a nonintegrable rank-two normal bundle, not a
contact structure or a second surface foliation. Its restriction to each spatial `S3` slice is the
contact plane `ker(sigma3)`. Twist modifies its clock component but is not needed to manufacture
the nonintegrability.

## 4. Global leaves

The distribution `E` equals the span of the complete commuting fields `T` on `R` and `Z` on `S3`.
The one-parameter subgroup generated by a nonzero left-invariant `Z` is a circle, acts freely on
`S3`, and has quotient `S3/S1` diffeomorphic to `S2`. Therefore the maximal connected leaves are

```text
R x S1,
```

one above every point of the Hopf base `S2`.

The metric owns the entire foliation because it owns the clock line and the unoriented twist-ruler
line on C01--C06. It does not distinguish one base point, one orientation of the circle, or one
winding. Reversing the ruler orientation changes the leaf parameterization, not the leaf set.

The broader family of Killing-flow surfaces obtained by flowing arbitrary transverse curves along
`T` is still query-dependent. The intrinsic leaves are precisely the special subfamily whose
transverse tangent is the metric-owned ruler line.

## 5. Complete leaf metric and reciprocal density

On a local leaf chart `(t,psi)`, the pullbacks obey

```text
sigma1=0, sigma2=0, sigma3=dpsi.
```

Thus

```text
h00=-u^-2,
h01=-a u^-2,
h11=u^2-a^2 u^-2,
det(h)=-1.
```

The off-diagonal term is retained. It is not removed by freezing the angular sector or silently
setting `a=0`.

The banked terminal evaluator is

```text
phi_pair=(1/4)log[(-det h)/h00^2].
```

Substitution gives

```text
(-det h)/h00^2=u^4,
phi_pair=log u=phi.
```

Equivalently `T=sqrt(-h00)=u^-1`, `L=sqrt(-det h)/T=u`, and `TL=1`. On these intrinsic leaves the
reciprocal-area condition is therefore a consequence of the supplied complete coframe, not an
extra normalization. The relative endpoint scalar is exactly `phi(q)-phi(p)`. Absolute
normalization of the unique Killing generator may shift `phi` by a constant, but cancels from the
relative depth.

## 6. What this does and does not integrate

Two endpoints on the same Hopf fiber lie on one intrinsic reciprocal leaf. Two endpoints with
different Hopf-base labels do not. Nevertheless the shared intrinsic Killing state defines the
endpoint coboundary `delta_K` across the whole R17 configuration. This endpoint scalar is not by
itself a connecting pair-surface Jacobian.

Within one leaf, different windings give the same endpoint scalar. They need not give the same
ambient or normal-bundle transport. For cross-leaf comparisons a connecting query/path must leave
`E`; neither the metric nor this audit selects one.

The vertical factor

```text
exp(delta_K X_lambda),
X_lambda=-P_u+P_n+lambda H,
```

remains a pointwise conditional metric class modulo screen `SO(2)`. The screen normal bundle has
its metric-projected connection, while full ambient R17 holonomy mixes the pair and screen and does
not preserve the grading. Therefore a complete four-dimensional comparison still needs a supplied
path/carry and a carried-to-intrinsic endpoint reset. The foliation closes the pair-surface seam; it
does not erase the normal-bundle seam.

## 7. Degenerate and excluded scope

This proof uses `u,v>0`, the regular global intrinsic clock/ruler projectors, nonzero twist for
metric ownership of the ruler, stationarity, and the supplied `R x S3` completion. It does not
cover null/rank-changing strata, twist-off C07, depth-off C08, other branch identities, or a
time-dependent metric that loses the stationary intrinsic clock.

It selects neither R17 nor any of the six supplied values of `lambda`. It supplies no on-shell
equation, action, source, matter, mass, bootstrap return, `X_max`, CMB spectrum, polarization,
signalling law, or dynamics.

## 8. Verification

- exact SymPy controller: 10/10 checks;
- constructive independent standard-library reconstruction: 72/72 checks over all six `lambda`
  strata and both Maurer--Cartan sign conventions;
- exercised mutation catches: 14/14 rejected;
- exact frozen source manifest: 15/15 source identities reproduced.

The first local independent verifier assigned the final bracket and leaf-metric coefficients and
therefore overstated its independence. Following external review, it was replaced by a constructive
implementation that inverts the coframe, differentiates that inverse, builds brackets from the
Maurer--Cartan structure constants, and pulls back the metric from tangent columns. The external
review's accepted landing was unchanged.

The topology statement uses the explicit global `R x S3` and Maurer--Cartan structure already
frozen in the source manifest; it is not inferred from the finite-dimensional symbolic controller.

